# Rename this file to harbour-readeck.changes to include it in the RPM.
# Add newest entries at the top.

* Sat Oct 17 2026 Contributor <contributor@example.com> 1.1.6-1
- Open links directly into Readeck from the system's "open with" menu
  (e.g. after scanning a QR code with the Camera app) -- not just via Share
- Fix: a link shared or opened while your device was still unlocking could
  be lost instead of opening the save dialog
- Fix: typed labels could be lost when using "Capture page in embedded
  browser"

* Mon Oct 12 2026 Contributor <contributor@example.com> 1.1.5-1
- Fix: after a device restart, you had to log back in even though you were
  already signed in -- it now unlocks your saved session automatically
  once the device is unlocked, no action needed

* Sat Oct 10 2026 Contributor <contributor@example.com> 1.1.4-1
- Your login is now kept in Sailfish's own secure storage instead of a plain settings file. If you were already signed in, nothing to do -- it switches over by itself the next time you open the app.

* Tue Sep 29 2026 Contributor <contributor@example.com> 1.1.3-1
- Add a setting to toggle justified article text on/off
- Settings page: server/username shown as label then value on its own line,
  left-aligned, with spacing between the two
- Article info page: reading time shown the same way, for consistency;
  "Links" heading now matches the other section headings

* Wed Sep 23 2026 Contributor <contributor@example.com> 1.1.2-1
- Fix a second, harder-to-hit crash on export for longer real articles
  with several images spread through the text

* Wed Sep 23 2026 Contributor <contributor@example.com> 1.1.1-1
- Fix a crash on export when an article has two or more images

* Tue Sep 22 2026 Contributor <contributor@example.com> 1.1.0-1
- Swipe left/right on the main list to move between categories
- Export an article as a formatted PDF, with images embedded
- Tap an image in an article to view it full-screen with pinch/double-tap zoom
- Article info page: long-press the source or any link to copy it

* Fri Sep 18 2026 Contributor <contributor@example.com> 1.0.0-1
- First official release

* Mon Sep 07 2026 Contributor <contributor@example.com> 0.1.0-1
- Initial release
